  <name>FontEasy</name>
  <summary>Install fonts on Linux the easy way</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Pick .ttf, .otf, .ttc or .otc files — or drag them into the window —
    preview their family and style via Fontconfig, and install them into
    your user font folder with a cache refresh.</p>
    <p>FontEasy validates every file before copying, never overwrites
    existing fonts, and reports exactly what was installed, skipped
    or failed.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.Silencio633.FontEasy.desktop</launchable>
  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Silencio633/FontEasy-Linux/v0.2.0/assets/screenshots/fonteasy-main.png</image>
